    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0156" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg98"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Romero to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 9, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>My <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> I have the honor to remit to you
                    copy, so far as touches the matter, of a letter which I have received to-day
                    from Paris, dated 19th of February last past, in which important advices are
                    given to me respecting the policy which the French government proposes to follow
                    in the affairs of Mexico. The person who writes the letter is worthy in all
                    respects of confidence, and the sources from which his knowledge is derived are
                    also authentic.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Seward, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi></hi>.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d43-a1.xml" xpointer="d43-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
